**The four HIGH findings, all in `target_snapshot.py`:**
1. A fifo, a link to `/dev/zero` or a large file inside `.git` makes the snapshot hang or use up memory. A 4 GiB LFS object used 4.3 GB of memory. This is the second report of this bug; the 2026-11-09 report already had it.
2. `compare` runs the target repo's `gpg.program` when a ref has moved.
3. A plain `git status` in a repo with a line-ending or LFS filter makes the next check fail, though no file changed.
4. Every snapshot reads every untracked byte. With 100k untracked files a snapshot takes 3.6 s, against 0.23 s before.

